{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>You have seen.</b> The vengeance that I inflicted upon Egypt on your account, and I carried you from Egypt as though you were carried on eagles' wings, for the eagle flies higher than any bird and all fear it but it fears nothing. This is the meaning of \"as an eagle stirs up its nest\" (Deuteronomy 32:11)—that it leads its fledglings gently. Also the matter of the cloud is like \"spreading its wings\" (ibid.)." "And I brought you to Me: My glory descended upon this mountain, and it is the mountain of the sanctuary. For Moses said, \"You shall serve Elohim upon this mountain\" (above, 3:12), and it is \"the sanctuary of Your habitation.\""], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:35:48.169570789Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}